@@ -16,4 +16,12 @@ Each setting is read from the process environment first, then from `.env` in the
 
 `.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines.
 
+Lines that cannot be parsed as `KEY=value` are ignored. Inline comments after a value are not stripped, so keep comments on their own line.
+
+## Diagnosing configuration
+
+`python -m payhook doctor` prints every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), plus which `.env` file was read. Secret values (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are redacted and only their length is shown, so the output is safe to paste into a support ticket.
+
+`python -m payhook check` prints `ok`, or lists the required settings that are missing, and exits non-zero if any are missing.
+
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
